From: Opal <opal@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] UDP 'reject' mode and DNS hijack for Tor

Tor relays TCP only. In 'reject' mode (socks5.udp: 'reject') every UDP flow that is
not DNS gets an ICMP/ICMPv6 port-unreachable reply sourced from the original
destination, so sockets fail immediately with ECONNREFUSED (QUIC falls back to TCP
without waiting for a timeout). Plain DNS to any resolver on port 53 is answered by
the mapped DNS, so names are resolved by Tor exits and never leave the tunnel.

Upstream: https://github.com/heiher/hev-socks5-tunnel @ e802f02
---
